---
import ProsePage from '../layouts/ProsePage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
const updated = 'August 24, 2026';
---

<ProsePage
  title="Editorial Policy"
  kicker="Standards"
  description={`How ${site.name} reports, sources, labels, and corrects its work.`}
  lede={`How we report, source, label, and correct our work. Last updated ${updated}.`}
>
  <h2>What this publication is</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} is a demonstration newspaper. The city of Port Meridian is invented, and so is every
    person, company, agency, team, and institution that appears in our pages. We publish this
    material to build and test a realistic publishing environment — page layouts, section archives,
    typography, and advertising placement — not to report on real events.
  </p>
  <p>
    We state this plainly because a publication that looks like a newspaper carries an obligation to
    say whether it is one. No article on this site should be cited, quoted, or relied upon as an
    account of anything that actually happened.
  </p>

  <h2>Sourcing</h2>
  <p>
    Within the fiction, we hold ourselves to conventional standards: stories name their sources and
    give their titles, figures are attributed to the document or official that produced them, and
    anyone criticised is given room to answer. Where a story turns on a contested decision, we
    present the strongest version of the opposing argument rather than a token line.
  </p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>
    Advertisers have no influence over what we cover or how we cover it. Commercial staff do not see
    stories before publication, and no advertiser is given advance notice of coverage that concerns
    them. Sponsored material is labelled as such and is written separately from the newsroom.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    We correct errors of fact promptly and visibly. A correction is appended to the article itself
    rather than made silently, and it says what was wrong and what the correct information is. If an
    error is serious enough to change the meaning of a story, the correction goes at the top.
  </p>
  <p>
    To report an error, write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with the headline,
    the passage in question, and what you believe is correct. Our
    <a href={withBase('contact')}>contact page</a> lists the relevant desks.
  </p>

  <h2>Bylines and authorship</h2>
  <p>
    Every article carries a byline, and every byline has a page collecting that writer's work. Our
    <a href={withBase('authors')}>contributors page</a> lists the full masthead.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of AI</h2>
  <p>
    The articles on this site are machine-generated fiction, produced to populate a realistic
    publishing environment. They are not the work of human reporters, and the bylines are invented
    personas rather than real journalists. We disclose this rather than leaving it to be inferred.
  </p>

  <h2>Reader privacy</h2>
  <p>
    We do not track readers. See our <a href={withBase('privacy')}>privacy policy</a> for what the
    site does and does not collect.
  </p>
</ProsePage>
